cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Indoor air quality dataset from a low-cost ESP32 + MP-135 + DHT22 monitor (Dhaka, October–November 2026)"
authors:
  - name: "masumkawsar99"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/masumkawsar99/indoor-air-quality-esp32-dataset"
keywords:
  - indoor air quality
  - low-cost sensor
  - MOS gas sensor
  - MP-135
  - DHT22
  - ESP32
  - TinyML
  - time series forecasting
abstract: >-
  46,897 readings (one every 30 s, 16 October – 1 November 2026) from a low-cost indoor
  air monitor in Dhaka, Bangladesh, built from an ESP32, a Winsen MP-135 metal-oxide gas
  sensor and a DHT22 temperature/humidity sensor. Includes raw ADC values, sensor
  resistance, a humidity- and temperature-compensated ratio, a relative Pollution Index,
  four air-quality classes, 2/5/10-minute-ahead class targets and a time-based
  calibration/development/test split, plus the training notebook and ESP32 TinyML firmware.
